    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0076" n="2" xml:id="pg2"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 6, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to my note of the 20th of October, and your reply of the 1st
                    ultimo, and to my further note of the 26th ultimo, relative to the case of the
                    Night Hawk, I have now the honor to enclose the register of this vessel, and
                    other papers duly legalized by the United States consul at Liverpool, for the
                    purpose of setting at rest the question of nationality, as raised by your note
                    of the 1st ultimo.</p>
                <p>In these papers you will see it distinctly stated that the Night Hawk was a
                    British paddle-steamship, registered in the shipping register at Liverpool, and
                    owned by Edward Lawrence, who appointed Captain Smiley, a British subject, in
                    command of the ship.</p>
                <p>I hope that the Secretary of the Navy will take these documents into serious
                    consideration, with a view of modifying his assertion with regard to
                    belligerents and neutrals, and look upon the ship as a vessel belonging to a
                    neutral power, and the crew, a list of whom I had the honor to forward in my
                    note of the 20th of October, as neutral subjects of that power.</p>
                <p>I beg you to return me the original documents as soon as note has been taken of
                    their contents.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d3-a1.xml" xpointer="d3-a1"/>
